20

Jim starts with 20 pieces of gum.

*   **Gum chewed during school:** The school day lasts 8 hours, and he chews a piece every 2 hours, so he chews 8 hours / 2 hours/piece = 4 pieces of gum at school.
*   **Gum chewed on the way home:** He chews 1 piece.
*   **Gum chewed after dinner:** He chews 1 piece.
*   **Total gum chewed:** 4 + 1 + 1 = 6 pieces of gum.
*   **Gum remaining before giving to his sister:** 20 - 6 = 14 pieces of gum.
*   **Gum given to his sister:** He gives half of the remaining gum to his sister, so he gives 14 / 2 = 7 pieces of gum.
*   **Gum left at the end of the day:** 14 - 7 = 7 pieces of gum.

Therefore, Jim has 7 pieces of gum left at the end of the day.

\boxed{7}

